            "id": "373450",
            "name": "Celebratory Kite: Butterfly Dance",
            "description": "A kite with a butterfly pattern made of bamboo, paper, and other such materials that can be seen at kite stalls during the Lantern Rite festival. Since one of the defining characteristics of butterflies is that they emerge from cocoons, they are often associated with freedom and happiness. Flying a butterfly kite implies breaking through constraints and pursuing freedom.",
