            "id": "370339",
            "name": "Curious Countenances of the Sacred Flame",
            "description": "A common type of open-air stall in Chuwen Fair, primarily used for selling masks inspired by the various tribal cultures. Low overheads make it a popular choice among merchants. As seasonal goods, demand for masks peaks during festivals and competitions, while footfall dwindles in the off-season. To address this, mask vendors have introduced a service that allows customers to create their own masks, offering a novel \"experience\" that has itself become a sellable product \u2014 after all, it's not something they're used to experiencing in their everyday lives.",
